Willow Rosenberg was feeling unappreciated, as usual. I mean her so-called
boyfriend Oz cheats on her with a werewolf, Cordelia stops talking and rolls
her eyes whenever Willow gets near, while Xander only has eyes for Buffy.
And
Buffy, Buffy gets all the credit for their adventures and attracts all the
cute guys, while Willow's just a sidekick that people only appreciate
because
she can do their homework for them. Speaking of which, here Willow did
Buffy's
book report for her, and what thanks did she get? Nothing! Buffy ran off and
became a demigoddess, without a word to her. What's more, she said something
like it was unsafe in the Mazes of Menace for someone like Willow. As if
she's
too weak to have adventures herself! Well, anything Buffy can do, Willow can
do better, she thought, pointing her chin up. Buffy may be a Slayer, but I'm
a powerful witch! I'll just have to have to get this Amulet of Yendor thingy
for myself and become immortal too! And any werewolves I encounter, are
going
to get the business end of an expert level Magic Missile. ;)

If above didn't make sense, this is related to the following game posted
earlier:
http://groups.google.com/groups?hl=en&lr=&selm=3fab9481%241%40news.microsoft.com
Willow is a Wizard, since that's so close to a Witch. She's neutral, because
she fights the good fight with her friends, but has been known to get into
darker magic when pissed off. Since Buffy came so close to Wishless and
Genoless, Willow decided to do it right. I was tempted to try (W)eaponless
for
a fuller "WWW" game, but Magicbane is so fun to play with, and is the one
way
to virtually eliminate baddies cursing your equipment.

Wizards are fun once you do the quest and your mana regenerates at about 10x
the rate, meaning you can actually play as a caster instead of a pacifist or
2nd rate fighter. Maze levels are actually fun when you magic map, followed
by
Detect Treasure to see what stuff you want to pick up, followed by Dig
through
any walls in your way. Magic Mapping or Detect Treasure is great for quickly
finding Ludios, or proving the lack of it in this game. With the Identify
spell, you can easily identify everything, so tend to have every valuable
gem
ever seen with you. There are so many options for dealing with monsters,
even
on no teleport levels. For example, if something nasty is next to you, you
can Finger of Death it, Teleport it away, Polymorph it, charm it, cancel it,
slow it, do tons of damage to it, Elbereth with an athame if you need a
turn,
and probably a bunch more options. With other classes there's a tendency to
want to conserve your wand charges, but when you have an infinite supply,
fire away! "So thou thought thou couldst kill me, fo--- *splat*" ;)
Mindflayers are more annoying though: Remember, getting your brain sucked
sucks (no pun intended ;) but getting your brain sucked as a Wizard is
downright painful (especially since it's avoidable unless you're careless).

The biggest game mistakes were made on the Astral. Famine (left), then
Pestilence (middle) were the wrong altars, but I managed to avoid Death on
the way to the right altar. Since Willow had something to prove, once at the
high altar I wanted to ascend with a bunch of pets. I know, you risk YASD if
you goof off around your high altar, when you should just ascend and be done
with it. ;) Anyway, I polymorphed a bunch of charmed ants into more
interesting critters, cleared all the corpses and weapons and such out of
the high altar room, and got to max hp/sp (the classic "polishing" before
ascension). Even with a magic whistle it takes a long time to get eight pets
(no saddle so can't try for nine) surrounding you. Everything was all ready,
when Death finally unlocks and comes in the door that turn. Hee hee I'll
stick my tongue out and ascend right in his face, and avoid fighting him
once.

But wait, on the astral you can't offer things on the floor (where the
amulet
was) like you can on other altars. Things went downhill from there, where I
was fighting Death while Burdened since I have to hold the amulet, lost
divine protection in the melee, while trying to avoid getting my pets killed
or replacing them when they get killed and getting them around me again.
After losing nearly 100 max hp, I figured it was time to ascend and be done
with it the next time all eight pets were in place (forget about other types
of "polish"). I cast sleep on some pets to keep them still in the right
places. But I forgot that unconscious pets don't ascend with you, so only 5
actually went with me. Oh well, immortality is immortality! :) Hi Buffy,
guess who! ;) Anyway, there are many more potential Buffy characters to play
with. Maybe next will be Giles the Archeologist, or Xander the Tourist? :)

